    {
        "content": "<p>Two  comments (neither of which get to the bottom of things):</p>\n<p><code>Γ(Spec R, ⊤) ≅ Γ(Spec S, ⊤)</code> is not a theorem statement -- it doesn't say \"these rings are isomorphic\" -- it is the type of all isomorphisms between them. Because it's not a theorem statement, tactic mode (which is for proving theorems) is not really designed for it, and although you might have found some edge case about <code>apply</code> being weird about unifying, <code>apply</code> was designed with proofs in mind rather than constructing data, which may be related to the error you're seeing.</p>\n<p>You say the error message makes it look like a reducibility issue, but to me the error message is saying something serious about universes not matching (the error says \"the second and third universes are the same in the goal but are supposed to be different by 1 in the application\"). This makes me slightly surprised that the term mode construction works at all.</p>",
        "id": 632259672,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1792156518
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I also thought it was a universe issue at first, but making universes explicit still produces the error</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">noncomputable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CommRingCat</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">})</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≅</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">):</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">R</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≅</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Spec</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊤</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"c1\">-- apply Γ.{0}.mapIso.{0,1,1,0} -- could not unify</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">exact</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Γ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mapIso</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">1</span><span class=\"o\">,</span><span class=\"mi\">0</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">φ</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">op</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
